## MUST

A — no finding message interpolates the containment helper's `error` any more.
I re-measured the helper before changing anything: a missing file answers
`{ code: "ENOENT", error: "ENOENT: ... lstat '/tmp/claude-1000/w110-err-.../ci/shots/W-110/board.png'" }`
and its own refusals answer `{ error: "path reaches its target through a
symlink" }` with `code` absent. So the two new sites switch on `code`:
`"ENOENT"` gives a fixed wording, `undefined` passes through one of seven fixed
refusal strings, any other code reports the bare code and nothing else. The
`ENOENT` wordings are chosen to carry none of
`/unsafe|unreadable|symlink|regular file/i` — "carries no screenshot manifest",
"is missing" — so a deleted file is one finding and a containment refusal is
deliberately two. 7(k) is rewritten as three writable assertions (an ASCII
range with a 160-character bound, no `/tmp` and no test-root substring, no
absolute path) and now holds against its own Genuine red, which it could not in
revision 2. The Interfaces paragraph names the contradiction that forced the
change. The nine-site class is enumerated in *Measured present state*, the two
adds are owned, and the remaining eight are filed as a follow-on with the
`code`-switch shape to apply and a warning that each one's wording is probably
pinned by a test.

B — 3(b) returns to revision 1's seven measured literal column ids, with the
coupling **stated**, which is what the original S8 asked for. Verified why the
derivation cannot work: `board.ts:9-13` makes `needs_you` a column with no
phase and `backlog` a phase that is deliberately not a column, while
`adapters/native/src/index.ts:40` declares `backlog` as a phase — the two sets
differ in both directions, so revision 2's row would have failed today on a row
marked "passes today", which Acceptance makes a builder stop. A correct
derivation would need `board.ts`'s `NEEDS_YOU_COLUMN` and its module-private
`BACKLOG_PHASE`, i.e. an export added to a file this brief lists as un-owned,
so the literal is the right rung. The row now names its own dependency (a
backlog opus gets a card in Planned; W-007, Planned head count 2) and *Stop
conditions* says a later opus that changes which states render owns this row
and that the walk must not import `board.ts` to paper over it.

C — behaviour 7 states **one** counting convention once, at its head: a count
is of `Finding`s as `checkStudio` reports them, so a message matching
`/unsafe|unreadable|symlink|regular file/i` counts two (`opus.ui.e2e` plus the
`opus.reference` `addPolicyProblem` raises at `:784-787`) and every other
message counts one, with the two-finding rows named — (d), (i)'s second half,
(j). 7(i)'s over-cap PNG and 7(j)'s over-cap manifest are corrected to two.
7(b) is one, and now says why: the `ENOENT` wording avoids the double-raise
substring by design, not by luck. Behaviour 6 points at the same convention and
records that none of its messages carries the substring, so its three "exactly
one"s are unambiguous.

## SHOULD

D — `validateServed`'s own gate-log read at `:675` takes `LOG_MAX_BYTES`
(1 MiB). Taken for the reason given: same function, same always-on path, and
a 2 GiB `ci/served.log` is the hazard just closed for PNGs. `:696` and the
other seven are left to the follow-on. The cap is added **without** touching
`:675`'s existing message, stated explicitly in *Files owned* as a deliberate
choice — an assertion may pin that wording, and the cap is additive on its own.

E — `code === "ENOENT"` is the literal, and `code === undefined` is named as
the helper's own-refusal branch that the switch must tolerate. The whole shape
is in a measured table in Interfaces rather than in prose.

F — residual 6 gains the tree-keying paragraph: every gate log is
`<opus>-<probatio>-<tree8>.log` (`pipeline/src/index.ts:99`) while
`ci/shots/<opus>/` is a fixed path step 2 clears, so a re-verify or a rebase
silently replaces committed evidence and nothing on disk says which tree a PNG
belongs to — which matters precisely because residual 16 has the operator
committing the directory. Filed as a follow-on with the reason it is not solved
here: keying by tree needs a retention rule.

G — both corrected: `http.ts:508-512` (verified: `serveStatic` begins at
`:508`), and the callers row now names `verify.ts:300` and the catch-fallback
at `:304` as the only `pipeline.run` sites, with `ci` reaching the pipeline
